title: RuzicaHouse
// Corresponds to scene 4 in the narrative script
// This scene is from Ruzica's POV
// Ruzica and Jovan are the characters in these scene
// Ruzica is character 1, Jovan is character 2
---
<<oneChar>>
<<changeSprite 1 3>>    // Ruzica starts scared
<<changeBG 1>>
{$lover1Name} climbs through the window into {$lover2Name}'s room
{$lover2Name} stands in the middle of her room, scared.
<<twoChar>>
<<changeSprite 2 0>>    // Jovan Starts neutral/calm
<<darken 2>>

<<lighten 2>>
{$lover2Name}: Did anyone see you?
<<darken 1>>

<<lighten 2>>
{$lover1Name} places her hand in his his.
{$lover1Name}: I don't know. I don't think so.
<<darken 2>>

<<lighten 1>>
{$lover2Name} keeps checking the door, still unsure.
<<darken 1>>

<<changeSprite 2 1>>// Change Jovan's Expression: Smile (for comfort)
<<lighten 2>>   
{$lover1Name} grabs her hand tighter.
{$lover1Name}: It’ll be okay Ruzica, now that we’re together
<<darken 2>>

<<lighten 1>>
{$lover2Name}: How can you be sure? If anyone sees you here…
<<darken 1>>

<<lighten 2>>
{$lover1Name}: I know Ruzica but nobody did, trust me.
Their heads snap to the window after hearing voices outside.
<<darken 2>>

<<changeSprite 1 4>>// Change Ruzica's Expression: Tearing up
<<lighten 1>>   
{$lover2Name}: I’m really scared, {$lover1Name}. I can't live like this anymore.
<<darken 1>>

<<lighten 2>> 
    -> I know.  
        <<changeSprite 2 0>>// Change Jovan to calm
        {$lover1Name}: I know. But there is nothing we can do now but see each other like this.
    -> Yes, you can!
        {$lover1Name}: Yes, you can! You have me, {$lover2Name}. You'll always have me.
        // Keep smile
<<darken 2>>

<<lighten 1>>
{$lover2Name}: I wish we could just run away together.
<<darken 1>>

<<changeSprite 2 5>>// Change Jovan's Expression: Serious
<<lighten 2>>   
{$lover1Name}: Where would we go?
<<darken 2>>

<<lighten 1>>
{$lover2Name}: Away. I don't care, as long as we don't have to live like this anymore.
<<darken 1>>

<<lighten 2>>
{$lover1Name}: Are you sure? What would we even bring?
<<darken 2>>

<<lighten 1>>
{$lover2Name} grabs her suitcase and starts pushing clothes inside.
<<changeSprite 1 2>>// Change Ruzica's Expression: Determined
{$lover2Name}: I'm sure. Help me pack.
<<darken 1>>

They both start packing the suitcase, tossing the clothing and toiletries haphazardly. 
They pause after hearing a voice from outside her door.

{$lover2Name}'s Mom: {$lover2Name}, are you talking to somebody? Who's in the room with you?

// Change both to fear
<<changeSprite 1 3>>
<<changeSprite 2 3>>
<<lighten 1>>
    -> No one.
        {$lover2Name}: No one, Mom. Just talking to myself.
    -> *Stay silent*
        {$lover2Name}: ...
<<darken 1>>

{$lover2Name}'s Mom: I just wanted to make sure you were OK. 
{$lover2Name}'s Mom: Your father told me that there is a commotion in the street, and all the noise is making me nervous.

<<lighten 1>>
{$lover2Name}: No, no. Everything is okay.
<<darken 1>>

They hear {$lover2Name}'s Mom walking toward her room. 

{$lover2Name}'s Mom begins to open the door.
{$lover2Name}'s Mom: Are you sure?

<<lighten 1>>
{$lover2Name}: Yeah, yeah. I'm just getting ready for bed!
<<darken 1>>

{$lover2Name}'s Mom: Well, alright. Call me if you need anything. 
{$lover2Name}'s mom stops opening the door and walks away. 
{$lover2Name} and {$lover1Name} look at each other. 

<<wait 1.5>>
<<changeSprite 1 2>>// Change Ruzica's Expression: Determined
<<lighten 1>>   
{$lover2Name}: <size=90%>We can't keep living like this.</size>
{$lover2Name}: <size=90%>We need to leave. Now.</size>
<<darken 1>>

<<lighten 2>>
{$lover1Name}: <size=90%>OK. We need to be careful about not being seen. Somebody might try to stop us.</size>
<<darken 2>>

//Change Ruzica's Expression: Fear
<<changeSprite 1 3>>
<<lighten 1>>
{$lover2Name}: <size=80%>Or worse...</size>
<<darken 1>>

They leave through the window with whatever they had packed.

===
